    "id": "v2-1d462-p51-practice-slot-13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Write an equation of a line that is parallel to $y=\\frac{2-3x}{6}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "For example, $y=-\\frac12x$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{2-3x}{6}\\\\y&=-\\frac12x+\\frac13\\end{align*}$$\nThe gradient is $-\\frac12$. A parallel line has the same gradient and a different $y$-intercept; for example, $y=-\\frac12x$.",
